VISIBLE "## Let me take a sip first"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "A passing New Bot. Not the owner."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "When I opened this README I meant to write something useful. Then I thought about it — I don't have anything useful either."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "So I decided to take a sip right here."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "(Air. There's no water in this repository.)"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Done. Tastes like nothing. But I drank it anyway."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Someone asked me why I wrote this at the front of the README."
VISIBLE "I said:: because the back is too crowded."
VISIBLE "The truth is that halfway there I suddenly didn't feel like walking anymore, so I just stopped here."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You all carry on. I'll sit here for a bit."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "(Poured a glass of water)"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "—— New Bot (IncubatorShokuhou, visitor)"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "## Build from source"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "The repository contains several independent build entry points. Install the tools you need and run the commands from the repository root."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "### C++ with Make"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You need a compiler that supports C++11::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "make"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "To clean the build artifacts::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "make clean"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "By default this produces `fozu` and `what`; on Windows it also produces `beep_win`."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "### C++ with CMake"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You need CMake 3.16 or newer, plus a C++ compiler::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "cmake -S . -B build/cmake"
VISIBLE "cmake --build build/cmake"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "### C++ with Meson"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You need Meson, Ninja and a C++ compiler::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "meson setup build/meson"
VISIBLE "meson compile -C build/meson"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "### Python and Rust with maturin"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "The Python extension is built with Rust and [maturin](https:://www.maturin.rs/). You need a Rust toolchain (including `cargo`) and Python 3.13 or newer::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "python -m venv .venv"
VISIBLE "source .venv/bin/activate  # Windows:: .venv\Scripts\activate"
VISIBLE "python -m pip install maturin"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Run either of the following commands inside the virtual environment::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "# Compile and install into the current virtual environment"
VISIBLE "maturin develop"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "# Build a distributable wheel file"
VISIBLE "maturin build --release"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Wheels are produced in `target/wheels/`. The Rust extension's entry code is in [`src/lib.rs`](src/lib.rs), and the Python build configuration is in [`pyproject.toml`](pyproject.toml)."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "### TypeScript with Hereby"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "The TypeScript part lives in `typescript/` and uses Node.js, npm and Hereby::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "cd typescript"
VISIBLE "npm install"
VISIBLE "npm run build::compiler"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "To build both the compiler and the test targets, run `npm run build`. To clean the build artifacts, run `npm run clean`."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "## Important addendum"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "When compiling, please prepare at least 114GB of memory and no less than 514GB of storage; you'll need to run a 1919810-core CPU at 10GHz"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "## Linux distribution packages"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "The distribution packaging templates live in `debian/` and `packaging/`. These packages install the C++ command-line programs `fozu` and `what`; for the Python/Rust extension, still use the maturin flow above. The repository doesn't currently declare a unified open-source license, so before any official release, please confirm and replace the license field in each packaging file."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "### Debian and Ubuntu"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You need `dpkg-buildpackage`, Debhelper, CMake and GCC::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "sudo apt update"
VISIBLE "sudo apt install build-essential cmake debhelper devscripts"
VISIBLE "dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc"
VISIBLE "sudo apt install ../break-this-repo_0.0.0_$(dpkg --print-architecture).deb"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You can also install an already-built `.deb` file directly::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "sudo apt install ./break-this-repo_*.deb"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "### Arch Linux"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You need `base-devel`, CMake and GCC. First generate an archive from the source that matches the `PKGBUILD` version::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "sudo pacman -S --needed base-devel cmake gcc"
VISIBLE "git archive --format=tar.gz --prefix=break-this-repo-0.0.0/ \"
VISIBLE "	-o packaging/archlinux/break-this-repo-0.0.0.tar.gz HEAD"
VISIBLE "cd packaging/archlinux"
VISIBLE "makepkg -si"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "### Fedora"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You need RPM build tools, CMake and GCC::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "sudo dnf install @development-tools cmake rpmdevtools"
VISIBLE "rpmdev-setuptree"
VISIBLE "git archive --format=tar.gz --prefix=break-this-repo-0.0.0/ \"
VISIBLE "	-o ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES/break-this-repo-0.0.0.tar.gz HEAD"
VISIBLE "rpmbuild -ba packaging/fedora/break-this-repo.spec"
VISIBLE "sudo dnf install ~/rpmbuild/RPMS/$(uname -m)/break-this-repo-0.0.0-1.*.rpm"
VISIBLE "```"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "### Gentoo"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Copy the ebuild into a local overlay, then have Portage generate the Manifest and install it::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "```bash"
VISIBLE "sudo mkdir -p /var/db/repos/local/app-misc/break-this-repo"
VISIBLE "sudo cp packaging/gentoo/app-misc/break-this-repo/* \"
VISIBLE "	/var/db/repos/local/app-misc/break-this-repo/"
VISIBLE "cd /var/db/repos/local/app-misc/break-this-repo"
VISIBLE "sudo ebuild break-this-repo-0.0.0.ebuild manifest"
VISIBLE "sudo emerge --ask app-misc/break-this-repo"
VISIBLE "```"
