VISIBLE "# Debian --a general-purpose operating system"
VISIBLE "[![Debian Logo](https:://www.debian.org/Pics/openlogo-50.png)](https:://www.debian.org/)"
VISIBLE "## Debian is free software."
VISIBLE "Debian is made up of free and open-source software, and will always remain 100% free. Everyone is free to use, modify and distribute it. This is our primary commitment to our users. It's free of charge, too."
VISIBLE "## Debian is stable and secure."
VISIBLE "Debian is a Linux-based operating system used on a wide range of devices, from laptops to desktops to servers. We provide sensible default configurations for every package and regular security updates throughout each package's lifecycle."
VISIBLE "## Debian has broad hardware support."
VISIBLE "Most hardware is already supported by the Linux kernel. That means Debian supports it too. Where needed, proprietary hardware drivers can also be used."
VISIBLE "## Debian provides a flexible installer."
VISIBLE "Users who want to try Debian before installing it can use our Live CD. It also includes the Calamares installer, which makes installing Debian from a live system very easy. More experienced users can use the Debian installer, which offers more options to fine-tune, including the ability to use automated network installation tools."
VISIBLE "## Debian provides smooth upgrades."
VISIBLE "Keeping your operating system up to date is easy, whether you want to upgrade to a whole new release or just upgrade a single package."
VISIBLE "## Debian is the basis of many other distributions."
VISIBLE "Many very popular Linux distributions, such as Ubuntu, Knoppix, PureOS and Tails, are based on Debian. We provide all the tools needed so that anyone can build their own packages whenever they need to, to supplement those not in the Debian archive."
VISIBLE "## The Debian project is a community."
VISIBLE "Everyone can be part of the Debian community; you don't have to be a developer or a system administrator. Debian has a democratic governance structure. Because all members of the Debian project have equal rights, Debian cannot be controlled by a single company. Our developers come from more than 60 countries/regions, and Debian itself has been translated into more than 80 languages."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "## PR template"
VISIBLE "This PR template can't really be called a template anymore; it should be called the :"Break-This-Repo Anomaly Containment Application:"."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You people took a repo that does nothing but :"automatically merge conflict-free PRs:" and played with it until the maintainer started writing::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Type:: kicked README / kicked docs / empty-fortress code failure / cat-caused incident / supernatural phenomenon"
VISIBLE "Verification:: I didn't touch .github/, didn't touch the protected README, no virus, no personal information"
VISIBLE "Declaration:: I admit I broke it, but I made the reason up, and it isn't even required"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Basically this means:: :"You can cause trouble, but don't cause real damage.:""
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "What is this template actually guarding against?"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "It actually draws the bottom line very clearly::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "· Don't touch .github/:: this prevents someone from blowing up the auto-merge workflow itself, or slipping a backdoor into CI."
VISIBLE "· Don't touch the protected README parts:: you still need a facade, and you can't turn the front page into something weird."
VISIBLE "· No credentials, viruses or personal information:: guards against supply-chain attacks, doxing and real malice."
VISIBLE "· Explain how to observe it:: you can pull a stunt, but people need to know how to watch your stunt."
VISIBLE "· Declare :"successfully made a breaking change:":: a self-deprecating disclaimer, equivalent to :"I did it, but I'm not responsible.:""
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "As for that list under :"supernatural phenomenon:"::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "three letters + three arrows around a circle + an outlined foundation"
VISIBLE "a world map on a pentagram background + a ring of crops around it + a five-word international alliance"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "The former is the SCP Foundation; the latter is probably some international organization like the UN Food and Agriculture Organization / FAO. Translated, it means::"
VISIBLE ":"This is no longer a code problem; we suggest reporting it to an anomaly containment organization.:""
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "How can your commit fit this template?"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "You upload the sources of Minecraft, OpenJDK and Fabric Loader, farming over 12.7 million lines in 4 commits; for the type you can tick::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "☑ kicked the docs"
VISIBLE "☑ empty-fortress code failure (cos Xu Jiayin)"
VISIBLE "☑ used Git cross-platform"
VISIBLE "☐ cat-caused incident"
VISIBLE "☐ supernatural phenomenon"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Tick every verification, copy the declaration verbatim, and for the reason just write::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Reason:: made up, not required, but 12,770,942 lines of code has to have a title."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "How to observe::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "Open OpenJDK_25.0.3, look at the commit history, and then feel the silence of the repository's size."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "But one reminder all the same"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "This kind of repository is a playground, not a lawless place. Uploading things like the full OpenJDK source or the Minecraft source may only result in a :"conflict-free auto-merge:", but it brings::"
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "· the repository size explodes, and GitHub may throttle or warn about it;"
VISIBLE "· copyright/licence problems — not all source code can be dumped in freely;"
VISIBLE "· if anyone uses this repository as a dependency, it's a supply-chain disaster."
VISIBLE ""
VISIBLE "So the conclusion is::"
VISIBLE "this PR template is the balance point the maintainer found between :"open destruction:" and :"preventing a real blow-up:"."
VISIBLE "You're welcome to keep playing, but it's best to treat it as performance art rather than a code repository. The SCP Foundation has already received the report."
VISIBLE "(This passage really reeks of AI — reviewed by HQ123-BOOP)"
